From decd41f77b02b802c4f70a2d5c48f5461ad4d1ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:26:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 43/45] panvk/jm: skip no-op barriers; GPU profile in apps
 without storage access

- A pipeline barrier whose second scope is only TOP_OF_PIPE (or whose
  first scope is only BOTTOM_OF_PIPE), with no layout or queue change,
  orders nothing, but closed the current batch. Yuzu-based emulators
  (Eden) record ~40 such barriers per frame inside render passes.
  PANVK_SPLIT_NOOP_BARRIERS=1 restores the split.
- panvk_env.txt is also read from /sdcard/Android/data/<package>/files,
  which apps without storage permission (Eden) can read.
- GPU profile: batch boundaries per second (BeginRendering, barrier
  splits, no-op barriers) and backend compiles over 5 ms.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_buffer.c | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c   |  4 ++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/jm/panvk_vX_gpu_queue.c  |  7 +++
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_instance.c         | 21 +++++++-
